\begin{align*}
50 &= 7 \cdot 7 + 1 \\
7 &= 1 \cdot 7 + 0
\end{align*}

So the inverse of $7$ modulo $50$ is $7$.  Multiplying both sides of $7u \equiv 23 \pmod{50}$ by $7$, we get

\begin{align*}
7 \cdot 7u &\equiv 7 \cdot 23 \pmod{50} \\
49u &\equiv 161 \pmod{50} \\
u &\equiv 161 \pmod{50} \\
u &\equiv 11 \pmod{50}
\end{align*}

So the smallest positive integer solution is $u=11$.  The next smallest solution is $u=11+50=61$.  The average of these two solutions is $\frac{11+61}{2}=36$.

Therefore, the answer is $\boxed{36}$.
